title: A repository with no commit yet: the panel lists the new files, the diff and a commit view do nothing harmful, discard with nothing tracked says there is nothing to discard and asks nothing, a file is staged, one change unstaged (it is untracked again), all staged, a staged file changed again and discarded goes back to what is staged, and the first commit is made from the app
folders: git-no-commits
expect-file: git-no-commits/a.txt :: ^a1\na2\na3\n$
expect-file: git-no-commits/src/b.rs :: ^pub fn b\(\) -> u32 \{\n    1\n\}\n$
expect-file: git-no-commits/.git/logs/HEAD :: commit \(initial\): the first one
forbid-log: script: ignoring
forbid-log: nothing offers

wait 3000
left changes
wait 500
mark 1-panel
wait 500
diff on
wait 1200
commit 0
wait 1200
commit off
diff off
wait 800
git discard
wait 800
mark 2-nothing-to-discard
wait 500
git stage a.txt
wait 1200
part unstage a.txt 2
wait 1500
mark 3-unstaged-part
wait 500
git stage
wait 1200
touch a.txt a4 written after staging
wait 2500
git discard
wait 600
mark 4-discard-asked
wait 500
answer Discard
wait 1500
mark 5-back-to-staged
wait 500
git commit the first one
wait 2000
mark 6-first-commit
wait 500
quit
